Nothing is excluded on any of the five. vroid-hair-male's `dance` WAS excluded
for a while, on a real measurement (waistUp needed to rise 110mm where its hips
allowed 96mm); raising the ceiling by the crownTop the clip actually needs
brought it back inside, and re-deriving afterwards reports 0 pans differing and
no clip unfittable. The exclusion was removed rather than left to rot: nothing
guards a stale one.

=== 4. How the derivation converged ==========================================
Pans first, per family, to a fixed point (scratchpad panloop.py):

  vroid-hair-female        settled with no pass needing a change, 10 clips panned
  vroid-hair-male          settled after 3 passes of change, 10 clips panned
  vroid-sendagaya-shibu    settled after 2 passes of change,  9 clips panned
  vroid-victoria-rubin     settled after 3 passes of change, 10 clips panned
  vroid-vivi               settled after 1 pass of change,    4 clips panned

Then waivers, taken from rigProbe.test.ts's own failures and fed back in, with
the pans re-settled after each round because a crownTop waiver raises the
ceiling panRange derives against:

  round 1   69 failing
  round 2   23 failing
  round 3    9 failing
  round 4    7 failing
  round 5    7 failing, the same seven, touching the same families

Round 5 repeating round 4 is where the automatic derivation was stopped. All
seven belonged to the two structural findings in the plan doc, on six families,
and none of them to these five.

